From fbeeef4c747294a11878018f5cefebf728b9118e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:09:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Serve CMPT_Read2 (0x1026) and NV restore from the working
 copy

MT6897 modems read their NV files with a handle-based compound op 0x1026
(open, seek, read, close steps; a handle kept between requests) and ask
for an NV restore (0x1021) of the IMEI file while booting. Answer both as
the vendor FS server does on a running Android, as observed on its
/dev/ccci_fs traffic:
- 0x1026: reply {completed steps, status} {descriptor +16 echo} {bytes}
  {data} {handle}; an absent file {0, -9} {..} {0} {} {-1}; reads see the
  modem's earlier writes (working copy) first, then the read-only original;
- 0x1021: Android restores the file from its NVRAM backup into nvdata; the
  restored file equalled the original. Here the working copy is reset to
  the read-only original and {0} is returned; the original is never
  written, an absent original is -9.
Offline test with synthetic files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mtk_ccci_userspace/mdinit.py | 122 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tests/test_fs_contract.py        |  40 ++++++++++
 tests/test_runner.py             |   3 +-
